        "mode": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "decay",
          "enum": [
            "continue",
            "decay"
          ],
          "description": "Two resume modes: continue - finish the original token/step budget from the checkpoint with the original schedule. Takes NO decay_* fields. decay - anneal a stable-end trunk checkpoint over an additional budget. Set exactly one of decay_tokens / decay_steps. decay_shape and lr_decay_to_fraction are OPTIONAL overrides; leave null to fall back to the schedule defaults. NOTE: decay restarts the dataloader from the start of a pass, so a resume-decay matches a single-run wsd decay bit-for-bit only when the trunk's stable->decay boundary is data-pass aligned; keep global_batch_tokens / world_size identical to the trunk's run. continue | decay"
        },
